Ported code: the ORCA grid generator
------------------------------------

meshom/orca/generator.py is a close port to Python of the tripolar ORCA grid generator of the NEMO ocean model:

- the original Fortran program by G. Madec (OPA8, LODYC, 1999), with the tropical stretch by A. Sellar (Met Office,
  2005);
- distributed with NEMO under the CeCILL licence (www.cecill.info). CeCILL v2 allows a derived work to be
  redistributed under the GNU GPL, the licence of this repository;
- the copy read: github.com/NCAR/tx1_4, folder supergrid/ORCA_gridgen, at commit 557efafc1b5a;
- the method: G. Madec and M. Imbard (1996), A global ocean mesh to overcome the North Pole singularity, Climate
  Dynamics 12, 381-388, doi:10.1007/BF00211684.


Methods after other work
------------------------

Apart from the port above, no code or text of other projects is included in meshom. Methods taken from other work
are written in meshom's own code and credited where they live:

- the built-in strait list (meshom/data/straits_fesom2_mesh_gen.json) and the strait, coastal depth and clean-up
  rules: after D. Sein (AWI), fesom2_mesh_gen;
- the rules that turn NEMO's ORCA grids into FESOM3 meshes (meshom/orca/fesom3.py): after FESOM3,
  github.com/FESOM/fesom3;
- the FESOM-C, FESOM2 and FESOM3 mesh file formats: github.com/FESOM/fesom-c, github.com/FESOM/fesom2,
  github.com/FESOM/fesom3.

External mesh generators (JIGSAW, Gmsh) can be run as optional reference baselines; none of their code is included.


Data
----

No data is included. Coastlines (GSHHG, Natural Earth), bathymetry (GEBCO) and NEMO grid files are read from where
the user keeps them, under their own licences.
